
const UPDATES=[{date:'8 September 2026',title:'The Career Update — Beyond Four Years',items:['Careers now run for up to 40 seasons: ten complete four-year Olympic cycles, with the Games remaining the defining checkpoint at the end of each cycle.','The end of every Olympic cycle now triggers a federation review covering Olympic medals, nation ranking, pathway delivery and records. Strong performance can earn a renewal; other playable nations can make formal approaches.','You can remain with the same nation or accept another national job and continue the same world, athletes, records, rivalries and manager history instead of restarting the save.','Manager profiles and the main menu now track Career Year, Olympic Cycle and nations managed. A 40-year career ends with a permanent legacy summary rather than after the first Games.','Long-save safeguards keep rival nations replenished without allowing the athlete database to grow without control, supporting ten-cycle careers more safely.']},{date:'8 September 2026',title:'Development Grades',items:['Removed visible numeric potential ratings from athlete management and replaced them with staff Development Grades from A+ to D.','Development Grades can be wrong: newly scouted athletes receive an initial projection whose accuracy depends on scout quality, then the grade is revised as evidence and programme knowledge improve.','Ability remains a staff range while PBs and official results stay factual, giving selection decisions useful information without revealing an athlete’s hidden ceiling.']},{date:'8 September 2026',title:'Athlete Profile Layout Polish',items:['Moved the national squad call-up / National Pool action directly underneath the athlete portrait so the control stays visible without competing with the rating card.','Reworked staff ability and potential range sizing across athlete profiles so wider scouting estimates remain fully contained inside their cards and development rows.','Tightened the mobile National Pool table so ability ranges fit cleanly without clipping on narrow screens.']},{date:'8 September 2026',title:'Rating Alignment Polish',items:['Ability/OVR and Potential/POT now use matching column widths, centred headers and tabular number spacing across Squad and National Pool views.','The athlete profile rating block has also been tightened so ability, potential and confidence sit on the same visual centre line across iPad and mobile.']},{date:'8 September 2026',title:'The Unknown Athlete Update',items:['Ability and potential are no longer shown as perfect numbers. Staff now provide working assessment ranges while PBs, official results and ranking points remain factual.','Assessment confidence improves through scouting quality, time inside the national programme and recorded performances. Newly discovered prospects carry much wider uncertainty than established squad athletes.','Squad, National Pool, athlete profiles, selection briefings, scouting reports, camps, Summit Series and first-day guidance now use staff assessments instead of exposing hidden simulation ratings.','Sorting by ability or potential now follows the staff assessment rather than the hidden true rating, so the interface cannot quietly reveal information your coaches do not know.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Athlete Profile Action Polish',items:['Squad call-up and National Pool controls stay beside the Overall rating but now use a compact, understated profile action instead of an oversized full-height button.','Call Up and To Pool actions use short labels, restrained status colours and a phone-friendly layout so the athlete profile remains the visual focus.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Faster Squad Management',items:['Call-up and National Pool actions now sit beside the athlete Overall rating at the top of the profile, so squad decisions no longer require scrolling to the bottom of the page.','The top action stays visible across athlete profile tabs and clearly shows when a call-up is blocked because all squad places are filled.','Programme Management now focuses on training load and squad capacity instead of duplicating the same squad-status button lower down the profile.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Nation-Aware Portraits & Deeper Name Pools',items:['Athlete and coach portraits are now assigned through nation-aware visual pools, so Jamaica, Great Britain, USA, Germany and the wider world no longer draw faces from one completely generic portrait rotation.','Existing saves migrate automatically onto the improved portrait logic, while future prospects inherit a nation-appropriate visual identity from the moment they are generated.','Scouting now draws from much larger nation-specific first-name and surname pools instead of remixing a small set of existing athlete names, giving the national pool more believable variety over a long save.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Mobile Interface Pass',items:['People Search is now reserved for the Home Screen so other tabs have more usable vertical space.','Phone layouts now use tighter responsive spacing, scalable typography and mobile-specific treatment for dense cards, tables, profiles, calendars, event views and onboarding.','Squad and National Pool gain a compact mobile sort control while the most important athlete columns stay visible without forcing a desktop-width table onto the screen.','Mobile navigation now includes a clean More drawer so every management area remains directly accessible from a phone.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Premium Presentation Pass',items:['Applied a full-game visual polish pass focused on depth, hierarchy, motion and tactile feedback without changing gameplay systems.','Main menu now has a more cinematic entrance, subtle ambient movement and stronger nation-themed presentation while staying clean.','Navigation, buttons, panels, tables, cards, dialogs, inbox, news, calendar and dashboards now respond more smoothly and consistently.','Improved selected states, hover/press feedback, lighting, shadows and page transitions across desktop and mobile, with reduced-motion support retained.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Main Menu Polish',items:['The main career menu now shows only the nation you are managing instead of repeating the Performance Director title.','Removed the High Performance, Strategy, Competition and Legacy footer labels for a cleaner, less cluttered menu.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Squad, Inbox & World News Polish',items:['Squad and National Pool tables can now be organised directly from their column headings, including event grouping, OVR, potential, fitness, form, fatigue and status.','Emails are automatically removed once they are more than four weeks old, keeping the inbox focused on current decisions and reports.','World News now includes a separate Social Media tab showing fan reactions, athlete chatter and trending names from the simulated world.','Social Media posts are immersion-only and never create World News notification badges.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Medical Reports & Email Badge Fix',items:['Inbox notification counts now update immediately as messages are read, so the unread badge reliably clears without needing another screen refresh.','Training injury emails now name the injury, explain how it happened, give the expected absence and outline the medical plan instead of sending a generic one-line message.','Injuries now develop as recovery stories with progress updates, medical clearance and a chance to return earlier than the original estimate.','Rare serious injuries retain the longer rehabilitation storyline, including setbacks, specialist reviews and a small chance of career-ending complications.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Race Motion & Instant Results',items:['100m runners now face the finish line and use a clearer forward-running body position.','Runner arms and legs animate only while the athlete is actually moving between race phases, then settle instead of running on the spot.','When any discipline finishes, the animation window immediately becomes the official final standings with the full finishing order, nation, performance and points.','The completed discipline stays open after the finish so you no longer need to leave the event and re-enter it to see the result.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Event Visual Polish',items:['Removed the location, LIVE/replay badges and broadcast branding from event animations for a cleaner presentation.','100m visuals now use deeper stadium perspective, starting blocks, improved runner figures, stronger lane detail and a more dramatic finish without extra overlays.','High Jump and Shot Put have cleaner stadium scenes, stronger lighting and shadows, improved athlete movement and more satisfying clearance, release and landing moments.','Event visuals now keep the focus on the action, athlete identities and official result only.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Broadcast Event Visuals',items:['100m races now use a full trackside broadcast scene with animated runner figures, visible race gaps, a live top-three graphic and a stronger finish-line moment.','High Jump now follows the athlete through approach, take-off, clearance and landing in a dedicated stadium view.','Shot Put now shows the circle, rotational movement, release arc, landing sector and measurement presentation.','All event visuals keep official performances hidden until the result and continue to respect reduced-motion settings.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'World Rankings Event Selector',items:['World Rankings now use a compact Event dropdown instead of a row of discipline tabs.','The selector scales cleanly as more athletics events are added while keeping the current event ranking, leaders and records instantly accessible.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Event-Specific World Rankings',items:['World Rankings can now be viewed separately for each of the six disciplines instead of one mixed athlete table.','Choose men’s or women’s 100m, High Jump and Shot Put from the event selector.','Each event view shows its own world lead, world record, national record and event-specific nation standings.']},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Calendar event colours",items:["Colour-coded event labels and a compact legend distinguish competitions, championships, camps, testing, league rounds, scouting and reviews.","Overlapping activities keep their own coloured labels so every commitment remains visible."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"First-day polish & season planning",items:["Compact onboarding, aligned offer buttons and seven-athlete starting squads.","National Pool and League Events now have their own menu entries; individual training stays in athlete profiles.","A dated monthly calendar supports scheduled camps, conflict previews and squad testing with separate practice marks.","Removed the automatic opening camp and its confusing email; squad lists now use the full width."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Fixed Commentary Panel",items:["Event commentary now stays at its original compact height, with text scrolling inside the panel.","New commentary scrolls into view automatically; earlier lines remain available by scrolling back."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Live Event Visuals",items:["Watch nation-coloured runners advance through the 100m alongside each commentary stage.","High jump and shot put now have animated field views, including the run-up, bar and flying shot.","Views support reduced motion, keep official marks hidden until the result and reconnect when you return to a running discipline."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Training Camps & League Circuit",items:["Book development, elite or recovery camps with clear costs, completion gains and competition lockouts.","Enter the six-week league circuit for three automatic rounds, separate standings and prize money. No Olympic or world ranking points.","Shared schedule checks prevent conflicting entries. Camp returns, league rounds and once-only prize payments arrive by email."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"People Search & Coach Faces",items:["Coaches now use a dedicated 30-face portrait pack, separate from all athlete portraits.","Search from any main screen for athletes, recruits, former staff or your manager profile. Results show roles and nations to help identify the right person.","A permanent My Profile shortcut makes your manager dossier easy to find. Sponsorship is unchanged; further refinement is back on the roadmap."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"People, Careers & Sponsorship",items:["Coach dossiers now show portraits, specialties, working style, reputation, contracts and a career timeline that retains departures and renewals.","Your manager profile records wins, titles, Olympic medals and records from saved results, with a personal name and evolving reputation.","Choose a seasonal sponsor: guaranteed funding, podium incentives or an elite prestige deal. Targets track new results and bonuses settle once at season end."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Coach Recruitment & Contracts",items:["Hire named coaches and support staff with different ability levels, upfront pay and appointment fees.","52-week contracts bring renewal reminders, fee-free renewals in the final four weeks and Level 1 interim cover after expiry.","Current staff levels carry over with a covered first term. Appointment history records hires, renewals and departures."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Facility Visual Progression",items:["Each specialist centre now has five illustrated stages, from Foundation to Elite.","Facility cards display your current investment level and let you preview the next stage before upgrading.","Artwork follows saved facility levels automatically and is embedded in the game for offline use."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Specialist Facilities",items:["Invest separately in the Sprint Centre, Jumps & Throws Centre and Recovery Suite, with five levels each.","Upgrade cards explain training and recovery effects, costs and remaining budget. Investment history and confirmation emails record your choices.","Existing facility upgrades carry over to all three centres. New investments are permanent and have no recurring charge."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Athlete Portraits",items:["Athlete profiles and squad previews now feature illustrated portraits from a 64-face collection.","Faces stay consistent across saved careers, squad moves, injuries and retirement. New scouted athletes receive a portrait automatically.","Portraits are embedded in the game file and work offline. The shared portrait collection may reuse faces across the wider world."]},{date:"7 September 2026",title:"Olympic Ranking Qualification",items:["Olympic fields now qualify automatically from season ranking points: 12 per event, maximum two per nation.","Qualification locks in Week 36 of Year 4. Injuries and retirements affect availability; overall rating no longer grants entry.","The Olympic screen shows provisional rankings and saved final fields, including national-pool athletes."]},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Athlete Traits & Morale',items:['Athletes can gain and clear Confident Competitor, Low Confidence, Training Rhythm and Feeling Overlooked traits through results and management.','Profiles explain each trait and show morale and recent changes. Morale has a small effect on training and performance.','Positive and negative trait updates arrive by email with clear icons; athlete links show active trait indicators.','Existing saves start tracking new evidence. Reopening results and messages cannot repeat trait rewards or notifications.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Athlete Rivalries',items:['Three close contests within a game year can establish a rivalry, including on the simulated world tour.','Athlete profiles show tracked head-to-head records and recent meetings; equal marks count as ties.','Commentary recognises active rivals when both compete, and new rivalries can make the news.','Inactive rivalries become dormant and retired athletes keep archived history. Existing saves begin tracking from new results.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Major Event Introductions',items:['National Championships, World Athletics Cup and Olympic Games now open with a distinct event-day introduction.','See the venue, stakes and your available entered athletes before opening discipline controls.','Introductions appear once per event, save your progress and never reveal results. Existing competitions already in progress continue normally.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Injury Recovery Stories',items:['Rare serious injuries now begin with a 20-week layoff rather than immediate retirement.','Medical updates track rehabilitation, possible setbacks and specialist reviews. Most return; rare complications can end a career.','Athlete profiles retain the recovery story. Serious injuries remain unavailable for competition and persist across season changes.','Medical clearance restores selection availability, with fitness and form to rebuild before a comeback.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'First-Day Artwork',items:['Atmospheric artwork brings your new office and the athletics track to life on arrival, appointment and week-ahead screens.','National-colour framing and readable captions carry your programme identity through onboarding.','Artwork is embedded in the game file and works without a separate image upload. Athlete and training-choice screens remain focused on their decisions.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Clearer First-Day Choices',items:['Onboarding now separates training instructions from scouting focus, with clear effects, trade-offs and timing.','Compare training approaches before confirming both instructions. Draft choices are remembered if you pause.','The final screen recaps your actual settings and explains where to change them. No week advances when you confirm.']},{date:'7 September 2026',title:'Email Type Icons',items:['Inbox messages now have clear icons and labels for selection, medical, scouting, federation, contracts, competition, reports and athlete messages.','The open message repeats its category, helping you recognise what needs attention. Existing save emails gain icons automatically.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'National Colours',items:['Your chosen nation now sets the colours of buttons, navigation, dashboard panels, profiles and the first-day introduction.','Great Britain uses navy, red and white; USA uses deep blue, white and red; Jamaica uses black, gold and green; Germany uses charcoal, red and gold.','Colours apply automatically to existing saves. Medical warnings and fitness indicators retain their familiar meanings.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Your First Day',items:['New careers open with a nation-specific appointment, a personal contract and an introduction to real athletes in your programme.','Choose an actual training approach and scouting focus, then see the next three milestones on your calendar.','A personalised first-week report explains the squad’s measured response. The introduction can be paused and resumed from Home.','Existing careers remain playable without restarting or being forced through onboarding.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Compact Home Dashboard',items:['The home page now centres on the next event and two compact panels: Programme and Athletics World.','Switch sections with labelled tabs, horizontal swipes or arrow buttons. Nothing rotates automatically.','Urgent actions remain visible, with full reports opening separately. Smaller screens switch between Programme and World.','New-update dots flag fresh panel content, and your dashboard choices are remembered in your career save.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'A World That Remembers',items:['Athletes remember selections, omissions, call-ups, conversations and career milestones. Trust has a small effect on training gains.','Explain selection approaches and respond to athletes who ask about repeated omissions. Replies cannot be repeated for extra trust.','New home panels show national objectives and the actual effect of each training week.','Young athletes gain gradual experience from competing. Debuts, comebacks and breakthrough wins feed profiles, news and commentary.','Pool athletes no longer receive managed-squad coaching bonuses in domestic events.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Scouting & Athlete Lifecycles',items:['Scouting now finds genuinely new prospects and shows discovery reports. Choose a discipline focus; existing athletes remain on the national-pool page.','Every nation gains new prospects over time, with extra discoveries at your national scouting events.','Athletes can retire as they get older. Very rare serious injuries can end a career.','Departed athletes leave future entries and free their squad places. Their profiles, results, medals and records remain archived.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Event Commentary Refresh',items:['Rewritten commentary across men’s and women’s sprints, high jump and shot put, with varied phrasing and discipline-specific detail.','Coverage now reflects field size, close results, athlete readiness, your selections and genuine performance milestones.','Longer reading time for each update; completed event screens retain the commentary for review.','Small and empty fields are handled without invented rivals or blocking the event.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Athlete Profiles',items:['Tap athlete names in the squad, pool, selection emails, training, rankings and results to open a full profile.','Explore Overview, Results & Form and Records & Milestones, with readiness ratings, season charts, coach assessments and Olympic medals.','Manage your own athletes’ training and squad status directly from their profiles. Rival athletes can be inspected too.','Individual performance histories now persist beyond the global results feed. Existing saves use available recorded history.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Squad Selection & Rest',items:['Unselected managed-squad athletes now sit out domestic competitions, including the Winter Throws Meet.','Only healthy national-pool athletes can fill domestic fields independently. Smaller fields are allowed when pool numbers are limited.','Selected, healthy squad athletes still compete as entered; previous completed results are preserved.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Coach Selection Briefings',items:['Selection emails now include a recommended pick, readiness concerns, an alternative and upcoming championship advice for each discipline.','Compare personal and recorded season bests, recent results, event ranking, form, fitness and fatigue on mobile-friendly athlete cards.','Advice uses your career data and flags limited performance history. Final selection remains yours.','World News notifications now clear when advancing a week, while newly generated stories remain unread.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Startup Recovery',items:['Added a fail-safe that quarantines malformed career saves instead of blocking game startup.','Removed the old startup decode failure path from the current master build.','A damaged local save can no longer prevent the main menu from loading.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Interactive Event Day',items:['Added a new Event Day overview screen for every competition.','Disciplines no longer play automatically one after another.','Start each track or field discipline individually when you are ready.','Completed disciplines save instantly and feed back into live event progress.']},{date:'6 September 2026',title:'Career Introduction & Startup Stability',items:['Added nation-specific welcome and job-offer onboarding.','Added the appointment contract flow before Week 1.','Improved startup and world-data loading stability.','Improved compatibility with existing career saves.']}];
