UPDATES.unshift({date:'8 September 2026',title:'The National Identity Update',items:['Great Britain, USA, Jamaica and Germany now begin as genuinely different management jobs, with distinct federation funding, facilities, staff strength, board targets and programme priorities instead of sharing one generic starting setup.','Each nation has a living Sprint, Field and Pathway profile. These values influence where future talent tends to emerge, but they are not permanent race-day bonuses and can shift over decades through facilities, coaching, athlete strength and pathway work.','The Home board view and Staff & Funding screen now show the current programme identity and federation remit, while the new-career and future job-market screens explain what kind of national programme you are taking over.','Annual federation grants now differ by nation, creating real resource pressure alongside different expectations. New or first-time national jobs restore that nation’s own infrastructure rather than a universal default.','Long careers can change a country’s athletics identity: a sprint-led nation can become balanced, a field programme can rebuild its track side, and the world’s talent landscape can drift across Olympic cycles.']});
