UPDATES.unshift({date:'8 September 2026',title:'The Athlete Independence Update',items:['Athletes now have their own personal coaches, competition preferences, championship-preparation preferences and working relationship with the national programme, making the squad feel like a group of elite professionals rather than federation-owned assets.','Athlete requests now appear occasionally rather than every week: they can ask for recovery, extra training load, a Summit Series appearance or protection from a lower-priority meeting before a major championship.','You can support or overrule athlete requests. Decisions affect trust; athletes with a strained relationship can occasionally hold their ground and decline a lower-priority meeting even when the federation wants them available.','Supported competition requests still respect normal entry limits and selection rules, so promising an opportunity creates a real management commitment rather than bypassing the selection system.','Rare personal or commercial commitments can make high-profile athletes unavailable for a Summit Series meeting, while athlete profiles now show the personal team and preferences behind future schedule conversations.']});
{const latestIndex=UPDATES.findIndex(u=>u.title==='The Athlete Independence Update');if(latestIndex>0)UPDATES.unshift(UPDATES.splice(latestIndex,1)[0]);}
UPDATES.unshift({date:'8 September 2026',title:'Nine-Place National Squad',items:['The senior national squad limit has been reduced from 12 to 9, creating genuine competition for places instead of allowing two athletes to be carried in every current discipline.','Brand-new careers now begin with only four inherited senior-squad athletes, leaving five open places for the player to shape through National Pool call-ups and National Squad Agreements.','The four inherited places are awarded to the strongest established athletes at career creation rather than guaranteeing one athlete in every discipline, so the opening roster contains real coverage gaps and immediate selection choices.','The four-athlete opening applies only to a new career. Later job moves inherit the existing programme rather than resetting every federation to the same starting squad.']});
{const latestIndex=UPDATES.findIndex(u=>u.title==='Nine-Place National Squad');if(latestIndex>0)UPDATES.unshift(UPDATES.splice(latestIndex,1)[0]);}
