UPDATES.unshift({date:'8 September 2026',title:'The Rival Nations Update',items:['Rival countries are now managed as evolving federation programmes rather than static athlete lists. Each has its own strategy, coaching strength, facilities, pathway quality, budget and current athlete generation.','AI federations invest annually, change coaching leadership, shift strategy after difficult cycles and develop young athletes according to the strength of their own pathway. Strong and weak generations can now emerge naturally over a long career.','International event fields now use federation selection logic based on readiness, form, fatigue, ranking evidence and programme philosophy instead of simply taking the highest hidden overall ratings.','Rival programme infrastructure now has a small real effect on preparation, while prospect generation follows the programme’s evolving sprint, field and pathway strength. The effect supports the simulation without becoming a permanent national race-day bonus.','World News now includes a Programme Watch showing leading rival federations and reports major rebuilds, coaching changes and investment. If you later accept a rival nation job, you inherit the facilities and financial position that programme actually built in the simulated world.']});
{const latestIndex=UPDATES.findIndex(u=>u.title==='The Rival Nations Update');if(latestIndex>0)UPDATES.unshift(UPDATES.splice(latestIndex,1)[0]);}
