UPDATES.unshift({date:'8 September 2026',title:'The Athletics Engine Update',items:['Introduced a shared competition-rules engine underneath the current athletics programme so future disciplines can plug into common round, advancement, attempt and tie-break systems instead of needing isolated event code.','Major 100m competitions can now use seeded heats and an eight-lane final, with automatic qualifiers, fastest-loser advancement and lane assignments recorded as part of the official event data.','High Jump now models opening heights, passes, three consecutive failures, countback and an unresolved first-place jump-off instead of treating the discipline as a single generated height.','Shot Put now runs as a six-attempt competition: three opening throws, a top-eight cut, three final attempts, fouls, second-best tie-breaking and reverse final-round order.','Event Day now shows the competition format before a discipline starts and preserves round/attempt detail with the final result. Official heat performances can count as recognised marks for records and qualification.']});
